{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-operational-entropy","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:operational-entropy","kind":"definition","title":"Operational entropy of the Reeb dynamics","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-reeb-operations-per-planck"],"tags":["information-theory","metric-entropy","julia-set","reeb-flow","hausdorff-dimension"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.operationalEntropy","text":"operational-entropy.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/operational-entropy.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:operational-entropy\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_q(z) = z^2 + c_q</code> be the quadratic iteration on the exceptional divisor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_c \\cong \\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{C})</code> (<a href=\"#rem:julia-set-reeb\">Julia set of Reeb flow</a>). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu_q</code> be the measure of maximal entropy on the Julia set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J(f_q)</code>. We define the <strong>operational entropy</strong> of the Reeb dynamics at substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> as:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\eta_q := \\frac{2q - 1}{q^3}.</code></pre>\n<p>This measures the information generated per <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_q</code>-iteration in natural units (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-bits).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/operational-entropy.md","heading":"Definition","number":"21.3.3"}
